// LZ4 binary - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// LZ4 frame: a four-byte magic, then a frame descriptor of two
// bytes and an optional header checksum.
//
// The descriptor's first byte carries the version in its top
// nibble, and its bits say what follows -- block independence, and
// whether a content checksum is present. The reader decides what to
// expect next from those bits, so they are not decorative.
//
// No free text: the rest is compressed. Hello World! is here.
//
// lz4_binary: 7 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 04 22 4D 18 60 40 20                            |."M.`@ |   <- 0000
